26-08-27T16:00:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133563656,imgsize-90422.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[North Carolina student to build first SparkNC VR learning unit]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133563922.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-lennox-french-the-north-carolina-student-who-designed-a-virtual-reality-classroom-idea-the-state-approved-it-and-he-will-now-become-the-first-student-to-build-a-unit-for-sparkncs-statewide-platform/articleshow/133563922.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-lennox-french-the-north-carolina-student-who-designed-a-virtual-reality-classroom-idea-the-state-approved-it-and-he-will-now-become-the-first-student-to-build-a-unit-for-sparkncs-statewide-platform/articleshow/133563922.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-27T15:18:15+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133563980,imgsize-103326.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Apollo 15’s Genesis Rock, found in 1971, revealed a piece of the Moon’s 4-billion-year-old crust]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133561078.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Apollo 15 astronauts discovered an unusually bright rock near Spur Crater on the Moon.  This sample, known as the Genesis Rock, is an anorthosite and about four billion years old.  Scientists believe it represents a piece of the Moon's primordial crust.  Its mineral composition offers valuable clues about early lunar geological history.  This ancient sample continues to aid understanding of the Moon's evolution.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-1971-apollo-15-astronauts-found-an-unusual-white-rock-on-the-moon-scientists-later-identified-the-genesis-rock-as-part-of-ancient-lunar-crust-about-4-billion-years-old/articleshow/133561078.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-1971-apollo-15-astronauts-found-an-unusual-white-rock-on-the-moon-scientists-later-identified-the-genesis-rock-as-part-of-ancient-lunar-crust-about-4-billion-years-old/articleshow/133561078.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-27T14:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133561241,imgsize-566227.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Australian platypuses rescued during drought quickly rebuilt their home ranges after returning to the wild]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133561771.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Following a five-month recovery from severe drought conditions, platypuses were reintroduced to their original habitats. In an eighteen-month study, researchers tracked their activities as they reintegrated into the wild. The animals displayed quick adaptation, rediscovering their typical movement patterns and preferred foraging spots, thereby emphasizing the importance of effective conservation efforts for aquatic wildlife amidst environmental stressors.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-severe-drought-forced-australian-scientists-to-rescue-platypuses-and-keep-them-in-captivity-for-five-months-after-being-returned-to-the-wild-they-rebuilt-their-home-ranges-and-resumed-normal-movements-within-days/articleshow/133561771.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-severe-drought-forced-australian-scientists-to-rescue-platypuses-and-keep-them-in-captivity-for-five-months-after-being-returned-to-the-wild-they-rebuilt-their-home-ranges-and-resumed-normal-movements-within-days/articleshow/133561771.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-27T13:45:21+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133562037,imgsize-2254146.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 2025, a US startup used ‘underground lightning’ to crack rock and unlock hydrogen]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133562765.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Eden GeoPower is investigating an innovative hydrogen generation technique by employing electrical pulses to crack deep-seated rock formations. This groundbreaking approach paves the way for water to interact with minerals, leading to enhanced hydrogen production as observed in laboratory tests. Ongoing field trials aim to determine the commercial feasibility of this promising method.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-2025-a-us-startup-blasted-hard-rock-with-high-voltage-pulses-and-made-it-10-times-more-permeable-now-it-is-testing-underground-lightning-beneath-a-massachusetts-horse-farm-to-make-hydrogen/articleshow/133562765.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-2025-a-us-startup-blasted-hard-rock-with-high-voltage-pulses-and-made-it-10-times-more-permeable-now-it-is-testing-underground-lightning-beneath-a-massachusetts-horse-farm-to-make-hydrogen/articleshow/133562765.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-27T15:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133563112,imgsize-2348512.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US college student shot dead by police after knocking on wrong house amid burglary call]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133564315.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-college-student-shot-dead-by-police-after-knocking-on-wrong-house-amid-burglary-call/articleshow/133564315.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-college-student-shot-dead-by-police-after-knocking-on-wrong-house-amid-burglary-call/articleshow/133564315.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-27T15:42:03+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133564939,imgsize-119712.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Yellowstone visitors used Handkerchief Pool like washing machine; cleanup removed 1.5 bushels debris]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133559736.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Yellowstone’s Handkerchief Pool was once a popular attraction where visitors put handkerchiefs into its water and watched them disappear and return. Its activity stopped after a log blocked the pool in 1926. A 1929 cleanup removed 1.5 bushels of debris, including over 100 hairpins, coins and a horseshoe.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/yellowstone-visitors-once-used-handkerchief-pool-like-a-natural-washing-machine-after-a-log-stopped-its-activity-in-1926-a-1929-cleanup-removed-1-5-bushels-of-debris-including-100-plus-hairpins-and-a-horseshoe/articleshow/133559736.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/yellowstone-visitors-once-used-handkerchief-pool-like-a-natural-washing-ma