c:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133556898,imgsize-90924.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[France heatwave: 10 Nile crocodiles hatch on their own for the first time]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133557283.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/france-heatwave-10-nile-crocodiles-hatch-on-their-own-for-the-first-time/articleshow/133557283.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/france-heatwave-10-nile-crocodiles-hatch-on-their-own-for-the-first-time/articleshow/133557283.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-27T13:44:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Prisha Roy</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133561993,imgsize-63504.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Why did Elon Musk get Ukraine’s Order of Freedom honour?]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133561095.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Elon Musk has been awarded Ukraine's Order of Freedom for his exceptional contributions through Starlink. This prestigious recognition underscores his significant impact on safeguarding human rights and liberty. Following the invasion, Starlink emerged as a vital communication link for Ukraine. However, Musk's decisions have also stirred political tensions, as he limited Starlink's accessibility for Russian forces and within Russia itself.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/why-did-elon-musk-get-ukraines-order-of-freedom-honour/articleshow/133561095.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/why-did-elon-musk-get-ukraines-order-of-freedom-honour/articleshow/133561095.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-27T13:33:32+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133561343,imgsize-33502.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[MIT built AI system to map extreme events that have never happened before]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133557503.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[MIT engineers have developed an AI-based machine-learning method that can create realistic scenarios for extreme weather events that have never been recorded. The system can generate maps showing the possible size, intensity and duration of rare storms. Using weather statistics and spatial data, it can model events that are more extreme than those in the training data. Researchers say the method could help planners prepare for extreme rainfall, floods and wildfires.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/if-new-yorks-worst-recorded-rainfall-is-200-mm-what-could-a-plausible-300-mm-storm-look-like-mit-built-an-ai-system-to-map-extreme-events-that-have-never-happened-before/articleshow/133557503.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/if-new-yorks-worst-recorded-rainfall-is-200-mm-what-could-a-plausible-300-mm-storm-look-like-mit-built-an-ai-system-to-map-extreme-events-that-have-never-happened-before/articleshow/133557503.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-27T13:08:28+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133559485,imgsize-262508.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[50,000 goats once ravaged Hawaii’s Kahoʻolawe island before eradication]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133559972.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1793-goats-were-introduced-to-hawaiis-kahoolawe-their-population-later-reached-about-50000-and-200-years-later-the-last-feral-goat-was-removed-after-severe-vegetation-loss-and-erosion/articleshow/133559972.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1793-goats-were-introduced-to-hawaiis-kahoolawe-their-population-later-reached-about-50000-and-200-years-later-the-last-feral-goat-was-removed-after-severe-vegetation-loss-and-erosion/articleshow/133559972.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-27T13:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133560132,imgsize-114788.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Montana landowner bought 2 mute swans, decades later flock of 120 threatened Yellowstone]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133559751.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-the-1960s-a-montana-landowner-bought-2-mute-swans-for-private-pond-decades-later-their-flock-reached-120-alarming-yellowstone-officials/articleshow/133559751.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-the-1960s-a-montana-landowner-bought-2-mute-swans-for-private-pond-decades-later-their-flock-reached-120-alarming-yellowstone-officials/articleshow/133559751.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-27T13:45:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133560493,imgsize-1693750.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[55-million-year-old penguin fossils reveal chemical clues about Antarctica before freezing]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133559922.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Ancient penguin remains discovered on Seymour Island are shedding light on the climatic transformations of Antarctica. Researchers employed micro-XRF scanning to analyze the chemical makeup of these fossils. High levels of titanium suggest significant weathering during the warmer Eocene epoch, while more recent fossils display diminished titanium readings, reflecting the continent's cooling trend. These bones act as an invaluable record of environmental shifts across millennia.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/55-million-year-old-penguin-fossils-reveal-hidden-chemical-clues-about-antarctica-before-the-continent-became-frozen/articleshow/133559922.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/55-million-year-old-penguin-fossils-reveal-hidden-chemical-clues-about-antarctica-before-the-continent-became-frozen/articleshow/133559922.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-27T15:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133560179,imgsize-599671.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[11,000-year-old sculpture of human seated on a leopard found at Karahantepe in Türkiye]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133557423.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Archaeologists discovered an 11,000-year-old sculpture in southeastern Turkiye. This unique artwork depicts a human figure seated upon a leopard's back. The 70-centimetre-high sculpture was found within a circular structure at Karahantepe. This discovery offers insights into early Neolithic artistic traditions and social practices. It adds to growing evidence of advanced capabilities in ancient settled communities.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/11000-year-old-sculpture-of-human-seated-on-leopard-found-on-a-stone-bench-at-karahantepe-in-trkiye-reveals-unique-neolithic-art/articleshow/133557423.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/11000-year-old-sculpture-of-human-seated-on-leopard-found-on-a-stone-bench-at-karahantepe-in-trkiye-reveals-unique-neolithic-art/articleshow/133557423.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-27T11:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133557591,imgsize-183238.cms"/></item></channel></rss>